{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons","id":889847,"title":"Ways to fix the nationalistic pantheons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-13T06:45:19-07:00","id":889847,"title":"Ways to fix the nationalistic pantheons?","content":"The ww2 nationalistic pantheons do not seem to be popular...to put it nicely with a lot of fans. I have been pondering ways to improve the original ideal of deities made out of national values or being the manifestation of a nation. Does anyone here have suggestion for ways to improve the idea? My idea is not that much better: A pantheon built out of nation manifestations like Britannia, Roma, Rodina Mat and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:49:50-07:00","id":889885,"title":"","content":"Those Gods actually have a place in Scion 2e, though it's a spot in the narrative (Columbia is a Scion of Britannia, who is herself a Scion of Athena, for example) rather than in a pantheon proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:40:10-07:00","id":890484,"title":"","content":"Is Marriane a younger Scion of Athena?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T22:21:49-07:00","id":893857,"title":"","content":"Most likely. So are Columbia and a lot of other national symbolic ladies after the Enlightenment. Let's just say ol' Athena met a lot of hunky boys around that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:55:01-07:00","id":894212,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that Athena would give up her Virgin Goddess status. Most likely she'd just adopt a bunch of promising women from gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:31:05-07:00","id":894279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons#post889847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ww2 nationalistic pantheons do not seem to be popular...to put it nicely with a lot of fans. I have been pondering ways to improve the original ideal of deities made out of national values or being the manifestation of a nation. Does anyone here have suggestion for ways to improve the idea? My idea is not that much better: A pantheon built out of nation manifestations like Britannia, Roma, Rodina Mat and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd strongly recommend talking to people from the countries those pantheons are from. It was quite clear they were based on stereotypes people from other places had about those countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:47:49-07:00","id":894292,"title":"","content":"Gods will be able to create Scions without getting involved in the floppy absurdity of human procreation. Athena, Artemis, et al. are not gonna have any problems that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:53:01-07:00","id":894296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons#post889847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ww2 nationalistic pantheons do not seem to be popular...to put it nicely with a lot of fans. I have been pondering ways to improve the original ideal of deities made out of national values or being the manifestation of a nation. Does anyone here have suggestion for ways to improve the idea? My idea is not that much better: A pantheon built out of nation manifestations like Britannia, Roma, Rodina Mat and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just be careful, okay? I have lost actual real-life friends to Hetalia fandom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:42:04-07:00","id":894415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894292#post894292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods will be able to create Scions without getting involved in the floppy absurdity of human procreation. Athena, Artemis, et al. are not gonna have any problems that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artemis actully claims pregnancy in part under her dominan, ironically enough. So I imagine she'd have no objection to conceiving Scions with WOMEN who catch her eye (they're carrying though).<br /> <br /> Athena purely uses adoption though - just ask Odysseus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:23:21-07:00","id":894451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894212#post894212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that Athena would give up her Virgin Goddess status. Most likely she'd just adopt a bunch of promising women from gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to run Athena as having stopped giving a shit about her virginity right around the Black Plague. Seeing as virginity is a &quot;virtue&quot; with which fathers hypocritically burden the daughters they're fond of, to keep them from ever belonging to anyone else, and Athena's father is the greatest slut in all of myth, she always knew something was off about her having to remain &quot;pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Athena is a Goddess of Wisdom and War, two things that don't actually go well with innocence, symbolic or otherwise. Once she realized feminism would eventually happen, she went and found a feudal lord who listened to proto-Germ theory from his Muslim and Jewish tenants and got her damn self <i>laid</i>, son. <br /> <br /> One of my players once caught her taking a man home. He asked her, &quot;Aren't you supposed to be a virgin goddess?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven't been a virgin since the Black Death, darling. I just don't let anyone <i>fuck me</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:21:13-07:00","id":894477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894451#post894451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to run Athena as having stopped giving a shit about her virginity right around the Black Plague. Seeing as virginity is a &quot;virtue&quot; with which fathers hypocritically burden the daughters they're fond of, to keep them from ever belonging to anyone else, and Athena's father is the greatest slut in all of myth, she always knew something was off about her having to remain &quot;pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Athena is a Goddess of Wisdom and War, two things that don't actually go well with innocence, symbolic or otherwise. Once she realized feminism would eventually happen, she went and found a feudal lord who listened to proto-Germ theory from his Muslim and Jewish tenants and got her damn self <i>laid</i>, son.<br /> <br /> One of my players once caught her taking a man home. He asked her, &quot;Aren't you supposed to be a virgin goddess?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven't been a virgin since the Black Death, darling. I just don't let anyone <i>fuck me</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it is certainly your right to play her that way but I have to look at a few things stopping that in my games. One, its in her very name, Athena Parthenos. And that is how she was worshipped for centuries so I imagine between that and her most famous temple also named for her virginity, the Parthenon there is more than a little bit of Fatebinding going on here. The other think I look at is that she specifically asked her father to be a Virgin Goddess, not out of some sense of superior morality but because as a virgin she would be <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">able to remain independent, unswayed by the spells of Aphrodite, the goddess of love, and the consequent pull of marriage and motherhood. One could look at her as the very first career woman...also watching the rest of her family being brought to their knee at the whims of Aphrodite was something she would have avoided.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:50:34-07:00","id":894486,"title":"","content":"Except that having sex doesn't automatically make a woman dependent on anything, and not all women [or Goddesses] want children just because they take lovers. I've played Athena as a strong, independent Goddess in my games, and definitely not a virgin,and that works for me and for my players. It isn't &quot;true to the myths&quot;, but after 2,000 years, even the Divine can have a change of perspective, IMO. To each their own.<br /> Edit: I'm not trying to start the old &quot;Virgin Goddess&quot; argument, BTW - I've been down that ugly, bumpy road before. I'm just saying, there's more than one way to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 05-19-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:18:46-07:00","id":894525,"title":"","content":"I mean - I politically agree with what your're saying about sex, I just think there are plenty of other goddesses to make that point with. I like Athena as an ace goddess uninterested in sex (after all, sexual empowerment doesn't require one to be sexually active, just in control. Athena and Aphrodite are equally sexually empowered, they just make different choices with that empowerment)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:01:08-07:00","id":894541,"title":"","content":"I guess my issue is virginity always felt very extraneous to Athena's purview. As soon as she got out of the Classical world and realized there was no need to &quot;lose one's reason in the grips of Eros,&quot; she pretty much decided her virginity was as useful as tits on a canoe, and was actively impinging on that whole wisdom thing. She's not some sultry sexpot or anything, she just has sex when she wants to, and doesn't when she doesn't. It's not a part of what she represents, and ancient Greeks worshiping her for it, to her, is a bunch of ancient Greeks missing the point of who she is. <br /> <br /> I understand the appeal of a more traditional Athena, or one who chooses to abstain because she has better things to do. I simply prefer one who doesn't feel compelled to tie her sexuality in with her divinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:37:17-07:00","id":894554,"title":"","content":"It's just a matter of what works for your campaign. There isn't any concrete reason why Athena [or any other virgin Goddess] has to stay a certain way after several hundred/thousand years of existence, if your story doesn't require it. Likewise, if it works for you to keep the status quo, then do what works for you. My only point was that sexuality isn't/shouldn't be permanently tied to concepts of independence or femininity or motherhood, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:42:29-07:00","id":894652,"title":"","content":"On the ww2 specific deities, i have used them as hooks for a bunch of stuff in my games, but as most people might guess, considerably tweaked/deconstructed them, working from the idea of them as false new pantheons created by a number of deities, from both within the &quot;Axis pantheons&quot; and outside it, to serve as a misdirection tool in their campaign of attrition against the aforementioned trio. Columbia, Brittania and Marianne were Athena under a series of disguises, Uncle Sam was actually a rescued and amnesiac Zeus, Baba Yaga &amp; Rodina Mat as &quot;rogue&quot; Vanir goddesses (the hag in particular being Elli, Goddess of Old Age, from Scion: Ragnarok), some were actually demigod-level scions and not real deities, while Madame Guillotine and the Citizen were actually dangerously smooth and stealthy avatars of a mostly unknown Titan related to emotions, social dynamics, oppresion, tirany and oppresion.<br /> <br /> Fun times overall.<br /> <br /> On the matter of goddess virginity, i would point out the case of Artemis, whose vow seems to be tied to her role in helping with her brother's Apollo birth in myth and also her relationship with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orion_%28mythology%29#Legends\" target=\"_blank\">Orion</a> that ended most tragically.<br /> Meanwhile, Athena's own vow does seem to have an element of imposition from Zeus part, but also the possibility that <i><b>the woman that she is</b></i> exists as a replacement of sort by Zeus of <b><i>the man that should have been</i></b>, what in itself raises all sorts of interesting issues. Beside this, there's the tale of Athena, Hephaestus and Erichtheus/Erichthonius, that in some of the archaic versions not only ends differently but has a far from unwilling Athena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:18:31-07:00","id":894758,"title":"","content":"The oldest version romanticizing Artemis and Orion's relationship is from a Latin source (Hyginus). There isn't a shred of that in the Greek. Hesiod's version, which Homer is consistent with, has Orion killed by Gaea (via a giant Scorpion) for his boast he would hunt and slay every animal on earth. No Apollo &amp; Artemis drama at all (he did have the honor of hunting with Artemis, but nothing romanticizes it).<br /> <br /> i am positive as possible, dealing with a culture that didn't have words for the concept, that Artemis' disinterest in men, and preference for the company of women, was originally understood to be exactly what it sounds like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:19:17-07:00","id":895300,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I played Artemis as a &quot;virgin,&quot; meaning strictly, &quot;untouched by man.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:07:23-07:00","id":901240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894279#post894279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd strongly recommend talking to people from the countries those pantheons are from. It was quite clear they were based on stereotypes people from other places had about those countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The personalities may have been. But &quot;Mother Russia (Ronda Mat)&quot; was an idea/ideal invented by the Russians themselves. Clearly an ancient Earth mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:10:44-07:00","id":901246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894451#post894451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I tend to run Athena as having stopped giving a shit about her virginity right around the Black Plague. Seeing as virginity is a &quot;virtue&quot; with which fathers hypocritically burden the daughters they're fond of, to keep them from ever belonging to anyone else, and Athena's father is the greatest slut in all of myth, she always knew something was off about her having to remain &quot;pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Athena is a Goddess of Wisdom and War, two things that don't actually go well with innocence, symbolic or otherwise. Once she realized feminism would eventually happen, she went and found a feudal lord who listened to proto-Germ theory from his Muslim and Jewish tenants and got her damn self <i>laid</i>, son.<br /> <br /> One of my players once caught her taking a man home. He asked her, &quot;Aren't you supposed to be a virgin goddess?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven't been a virgin since the Black Death, darling. I just don't let anyone <i>fuck me</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, the Goddess of Wisdom would know how to be sexual and not get CAUGHT!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T18:33:05-07:00","id":902416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=901240#post901240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The personalities may have been. But &quot;Mother Russia (Ronda Mat)&quot; was an idea/ideal invented by the Russians themselves. Clearly an ancient Earth mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the personalities. I mean who in Britain or France think of Robin Hood and d'Artagnan as tutelary spirits or divine figures? Why not put Tom Sawyer or Scarlet O'hara in the Yankee pantheon while we're at it?<br /> I think the meaning and importance of those figures may not be the same when seen from their home countries as they are viewed from outside.<br /> <br /> D'Artagnan is a popular litterary character for example, but in no way representative of the French national spirit. He is a proudly Gascon stereotype, an expression of a powerful regional identity, more than he is national rallying point. I guess the same could be said of B'rer Rabbit, but in his case, he's at least a genuine folkloric figure, an ubiquitous archetype with ties to a deeper mythology. Roland, Aub\u00e9ron, M\u00e9lusine or even Gargantua would probably have been closer equivalents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:14:23-07:00","id":902439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=902416#post902416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean who in Britain or France think of Robin Hood and d'Artagnan as tutelary spirits or divine figures?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*blink* Who in the United States thinks that Bette Ross or Uncle Sam or Amelia Earhart are tutelary spirits or divine figures?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I like the national pantheons - I don't. But the idea that they didn't apply the same ridiculousness to the American set is just blatantly false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T04:02:14-07:00","id":902608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=902439#post902439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *blink* Who in the United States thinks that Bette Ross or Uncle Sam or Amelia Earhart are tutelary spirits or divine figures?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I like the national panthons - I don't. But the idea that they didn't apply the same ridiculousness to the American set is just blatantly false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not saying that the Yankee pantheon does or doesn't suffer from the same flaw; I have no mean to know, which is my point. I'm not familiar enough with US folklore and culture to know what these characters mean.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:26:08-07:00","id":902833,"title":"","content":"I'd actually thought of some ways to fix the Yankee Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Uncle Sam isn't <i>The</i> Uncle Sam. He's a Scion who took &quot;embodiment of the ideals of the United States of America&quot; as one of his mantles, and Uncle Sam just happens to be a convenient role to assume for that mantle.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Rosie the Riveter isn't really Rosie the Riveter. She is a scion turned God of Female Empowerment, Women's rights, and women who work who took Rosie as one of her Mantles.<br /> <br /> Drop Betsy Ross. The real Betsy Ross didn't even sew the flag they say she sewed. She really only seems to be their as a excuse to have a god of &quot;Mom and Apple Pie.&quot; If you want that, replace her with a Scion turned Goddess of Mom and Apple Pie who calls herself &quot;Mom&quot; and drop the Betsy Ross connection entirely.<br /> <br /> Br'er Rabbit is a combination of trickster characters from African and Cherokee Folklore. If he is a god in his own right, as opposed to one of those tricksters mantling the other or just a diferant name for one of them,then he belongs in one or both of those pantheons, either instead of or in addition to the Yankees.<br /> <br /> Columbia is fine as a scion or grand scion of Athena who was either adopted by another Yankee or joined it as a god.<br /> <br /> That leaves us with Pecos Bill, Paul Bunyan, John Henry, and Johnny Appleseed. These are either characters from Tall Tales, or they're real people who inspired tall tales. They're all scions, the Tall Tales were their heroic journeys which then inspired their legends, and they all became gods towards the end of the story's/their lives.<br /> <br /> I'd also make it very, very clear that the Yankee's a young Pantheon, even younger than the nation that they're gods of. Hell, maybe even use them as an example of a bunch of Scions getting together to form their own pantheon when it's time to write the rules for that?<br /> <br /> Industry is no longer the Panthein Specific Purview, though industrial Elements might be in the new one. Instead, Industry is an application of crafting purviews...I still like the &quot;Divine Nuke&quot; Boon though. That'd need to be reworked and incorporated somehow.<br /> <br /> The Allied Pantheons could work similarly, but break the up into individual Pantheons instead all being the same, and for Fucks sake, where is King Arthur?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:56:57-07:00","id":903031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons#post889847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ww2 nationalistic pantheons do not seem to be popular...to put it nicely with a lot of fans. I have been pondering ways to improve the original ideal of deities made out of national values or being the manifestation of a nation. Does anyone here have suggestion for ways to improve the idea? My idea is not that much better: A pantheon built out of nation manifestations like Britannia, Roma, Rodina Mat and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Considering how Brer Rabbit is an alter ego for Coyote, who is a Native American deity? I would suggest adding the rest of that respective pantheon to the list. Or at least one tribe's collective version of it, as I'm not sure if they had religious diversity among the natives.<br /> <br /> I think the major problem people had with the nationalist pantheons was that it seemed to just be a grab bag of random folk heroes, rather than being a coherent pantheon. The Allied Pantheon, for example, was extremely limited with only 3 legendary figures from each nation working together. I know it said they suffered heavy loses, which prompted them to form an alliance, but I think we can give them more credit than that.<br /> <br /> I've heard a couple people suggest that for the British pantheon, you use King Arthur mythology, since it's actually quite popular in their country. <i>Also, who wouldn't want to be the Scion of Merlin?</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=894477#post894477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it is certainly your right to play her that way but I have to look at a few things stopping that in my games. One, its in her very name, Athena Parthenos. And that is how she was worshipped for centuries so I imagine between that and her most famous temple also named for her virginity, the Parthenon there is more than a little bit of Fatebinding going on here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, if I'm not mistaken, it was somewhere on these very forums discussing virgin deities. Somebody pointed out that the ancient Greeks did not consider same sex coupling to be intercourse. So just because Athena / Artemis may be described as &quot;virgins&quot; doesn't strictly mean they haven't bedded anyone. In fact, I believe the Hero book states that Artemis <i>prefers the companionship of women</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to ancient Greece, they may have been called virgins. But to modern civilization, we'd call them lesbians! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-29-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T15:07:50-07:00","id":903035,"title":"","content":"<b>Delete, Please</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Added the two posts together to save space. 05-29-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:04:51-07:00","id":903252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=903031#post903031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, if I'm not mistaken, it was somewhere on these very forums discussing virgin deities. Somebody pointed out that the ancient Greeks did not consider same sex coupling to be intercourse. So just because Athena / Artemis may be described as &quot;virgins&quot; doesn't strictly mean they haven't bedded anyone. In fact, I believe the Hero book states that Artemis <i>prefers the companionship of women</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to ancient Greece, they may have been called virgins. But to modern civilization, we'd call them lesbians! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would not have considered same sex <i><b>female</b></i> coupling to be intercourse.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you want to take that route with Athena I've got no problem with it at all (Xena: Warrior Princess presented her as a lesbian in the arc following the death of Zeus when Athena was leading the Olympian response against Xena and her daughter). That said, in the interest of being informative, I will point out there is less foundation in myth for it than with Artemis. Artemis forswearing the touch of man was a promise she specifically extracts from Zeus so she can run off with solely the company of women, and there's a whole list of maidens who are &quot;favored&quot; by Artemis to join her company. By contrast, Athena rarely has any positive interaction with other women in mythology (part of this is reflective of patriarchal values of the Ancient Greeks of course - it is a show of respect to Athena to treat her &quot;like a man&quot; and unconcerned with women &amp; &quot;womanly things&quot;... other than the outlier of weaving).<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'm all for shedding or deconstructing that misogyny in modern adaptations. I'm just saying I don't think the Ancient Greeks understood Athena to &quot;prefer the company of women&quot; the way they understood Artemis to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-30-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:13:58-07:00","id":903257,"title":"","content":"Of course when we talk about &quot;Greek Myth&quot; let's be honest: we mean Athenian Myth. It is entirely plausible that if we had Spartan records of their legends, we'd have lineages of hero-kings descending from heterosexual coupling by Artemis, Ares would be a noble general like Mars rather than a bloodthirsty craven, and Athena would be primarily a goddess of &quot;womanly crafts&quot;. But we don't have those myths and will likely never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:19:39-07:00","id":903631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=902833#post902833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Drop Betsy Ross. The real Betsy Ross didn't even sew the flag they say she sewed. She really only seems to be their as a excuse to have a god of &quot;Mom and Apple Pie.&quot; If you want that, replace her with a Scion turned Goddess of Mom and Apple Pie who calls herself &quot;Mom&quot; and drop the Betsy Ross connection entirely.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, better yet, make them into a twin deity and call them &quot;Mom and Pop.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:04:59-07:00","id":903825,"title":"","content":"Only reason I can see for King Arthur not being there is the whole 'Rise from Avalon at Britain's greatest need' thing, although if WWII wasn't Britain's greatest need, that has some unfortunate implications for the British isles in the scion setting. Hey that could be a good nation pantheon or Tuatha plot hook right there, figure out why WWII wasn't the time of greatest need and what lies ahead, heck you could even base an entire campaign in Britain with that concept if you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:49:27-07:00","id":903873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=903252#post903252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would not have considered same sex <i><b>female</b></i> coupling to be intercourse.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you want to take that route with Athena I've got no problem with it at all (Xena: Warrior Princess presented her as a lesbian in the arc following the death of Zeus when Athena was leading the Olympian response against Xena and her daughter). That said, in the interest of being informative, I will point out there is less foundation in myth for it than with Artemis. Artemis forswearing the touch of man was a promise she specifically extracts from Zeus so she can run off with solely the company of women, and there's a whole list of maidens who are &quot;favored&quot; by Artemis to join her company. By contrast, Athena rarely has any positive interaction with other women in mythology (part of this is reflective of patriarchal values of the Ancient Greeks of course - it is a show of respect to Athena to treat her &quot;like a man&quot; and unconcerned with women &amp; &quot;womanly things&quot;... other than the outlier of weaving).<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'm all for shedding or deconstructing that misogyny in modern adaptations. I'm just saying I don't think the Ancient Greeks understood Athena to &quot;prefer the company of women&quot; the way they understood Artemis to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much agree with everything here.<br /> <br /> Even the weaving was more a Roman than Greek thing.<br /> <br /> As you mentioned, Artemis was described pretty explicitely as a lesbian, but as far as I know Athena was never said to have had a willing sexual contact with anyone. The only references to anything sexual concerning her I can recall is her asking Zeus to allow her to remain a virgin, and Hephaestos trying to rape her.<br /> <br /> Really I don't see why she and Hestia couldn't be asexual. It seems especially fitting for the daughter of the first goddes of wisdom, born from her father's brains, to be less interested in matters of the flesh than other olympians. Making Athena sexual seems to go contrary to her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:11:50-07:00","id":904028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=903873#post903873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Really I don't see why she and Hestia couldn't be asexual. It seems especially fitting for the daughter of the first goddes of wisdom, born from her father's brains, to be less interested in matters of the flesh than other olympians. Making Athena sexual seems to go contrary to her character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My theory is that after spending all that time inside Zeus' head, she had seen enough sex to last a life time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:15:41-07:00","id":904167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=903873#post903873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the weaving was more a Roman than Greek thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The authors (Ovid and Virgil) were Roman, but that doesn't make the material Roman in the slightest. Both were working from Hellenistic sources (which are largely gone - the burning of the Library of Alexandria, the Dark Ages, et al.) and weren't creating this stuff from whole cloth (an inadvertent pun). In fact, they WOULDN'T have. This isn't creative writing, it's an effort to take extant (Greek) stories and bring them together in a way that makes the author's point. The fact that the story of Athena and Arachne is takes place in Greek locations, Greek names (it's not Arananea, it's Arachne and even though he says &quot;Minerva&quot; he says &quot;Pallas Minerva&quot;, and Pallas is a Greek epithet) and involves Greek themes (like Athena's choice of topic for her tapestry) indicates this is not a Roman story.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:27:16-07:00","id":904216,"title":"","content":"So - does the sexuality of any other Goddesses ever come up in games, or is it just that there's a fascination with the sexual activity [or lack of it] of Athena and Artemis? And is it really relevant to their worship, past, present or in-game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:37:08-07:00","id":904265,"title":"","content":"I have to say that I find it interesting when I read many posts about updating gods like Athena and Artemis, completely changing their personalities from what the ancient Greeks had them written like in their myths\u2026it\u2019s almost like saving them from ancient views on women and attitudes towards sex; citing various modern interpretations (that are highly inaccurate but fun re-imagining\u2019s like Xena or Disney) as being the inspiration for this \u2018better\u2019 version of the god in question. <br /> <br /> The same isn\u2019t done for gods like Zeus or Hades. Zeus is just a dick. Despite being fairly brilliant himself, he never learns in seven thousand years, never grows out of the baser character flaws he has\u2026in fact most people only remember his flaws when thinking or referring to him. It\u2019s like Fatebinding applies to him and keeps him like that (personally because I think many love to hate him) but not to the gods that people like. <br /> <br /> Hades gets pretty much transformed/conflated into Satan in almost every modern appearance he makes and his realm becomes Hell. Set got vilified because of Marvel comics and somehow no one remembers that he is Ra\u2019s protector/guardian on the barge. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:33:23-07:00","id":904395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=904216#post904216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So - does the sexuality of any other Goddesses ever come up in games, or is it just that there's a fascination with the sexual activity [or lack of it] of Athena and Artemis? And is it really relevant to their worship, past, present or in-game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they're the only goddesses who are explicitly discussed as being virgins. There are male deities who don't have sex, but that's usually because they've been castrated, or are otherwise too hideous to attract a willing partner.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the Hindu goddesses is also described as refraining from sex, but that's because she's already lovingly married to another member of the pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:38:53-07:00","id":904400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=904265#post904265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hades gets pretty much transformed/conflated into Satan in almost every modern appearance he makes and his realm becomes Hell. Set got vilified because of Marvel comics and somehow no one remembers that he is Ra\u2019s protector/guardian on the barge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it always aggravates me that people keep portraying one of the most well behaved deities of ancient Greece to be some kind of demonic tyrant, and they constantly forget that Hades' realm wasn't just endless fire and brimstone.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know what Marvel did to Set, but they completely mislead me about Loki. It wasn't until I started asking around here that I learned he was Odin's brother (not Thor's), and that he and Thor are actually good friends!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:24:27-07:00","id":904446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=904167#post904167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, they WOULDN'T have. This isn't creative writing</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely invented a ton of stuff and tied it back to Hellenistic contexts to give it foundation. The entire point of the Aenid was to give Rome a NEW founding myth that wasn't a political threat Augustus - given that the Romulus and Remus story was being used as a thinly veiled accusation that he killed his his &quot;brother&quot; Caesarion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:42:44-07:00","id":904463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=904265#post904265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say that I find it interesting when I read many posts about updating gods like Athena and Artemis, completely changing their personalities from what the ancient Greeks had them written like in their myths\u2026it\u2019s almost like saving them from ancient views on women and attitudes towards sex; citing various modern interpretations (that are highly inaccurate but fun re-imagining\u2019s like Xena or Disney) as being the inspiration for this \u2018better\u2019 version of the god in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I sited Xena in a post specifically about how Athena-as-gay LACKS mythic foundation (unlike Artemis-as-gay, which has a ton of mythic foundation). I'm on team &quot;Athena as virgin in modern meaning&quot;<br /> <br /> As to her negative traits the Ancient Greeks projected onto her as positive in their misogyny, I don't think those should necessarily be dropped, just deconstructed. Athena can absolutely as a character flaw be presented with &quot;not like other girls/women are ditzy and stupid/I'm one of the guys&quot;. internalized misogyny and be 100% accurate to the myths while being a modern critique there-of.<br /> <br /> On Hades, obviously he's not Satan, that's a Christian moral dualist imposition on the myths. We all know that.<br /> <br /> Sutekh is more complicated, because you are right he is a defender of Re and that tends to be forgotten, but he was vilified by Ancient Egyptian Cults LONG before Marvel Comics came along. He was always the God of Desert barbarians and thus their enemies, and his most narratively central myth is his murder of Azar and attempted usurpation of Heru.<br /> <br /> I actually have an idea on that that ties in with his loyalty to Re and makes him more morally ambiguous, with Aset being an equally ambiguous political master-manipulator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-01-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:43:51-07:00","id":904466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889847-ways-to-fix-the-nationalistic-pantheons?p=904216#post904216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So - does the sexuality of any other Goddesses ever come up in games, or is it just that there's a fascination with the sexual activity [or lack of it] of Athena and Artemis? And is it really relevant to their worship, past, present or in-game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It just comes up with &quot;virgin goddesses&quot; because of the question of playing their Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:04:54-07:00","id":904482,"title":"","content":"That said Achilles, these were living myths that the Greeks and Romans were constantly inventing and reinventing, not revealed dogma, so continuing to reinterpreting/reinventing them in our social context can be argued to be in keeping with that tradition far more than treating the &quot;original&quot; as objective and unchanging would be. these stories come to us through entertainment-storytellers, not priests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}